course: dictionary
lesson: 3471
title: Faithfulness: loyal and true
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Faithfulness is a noun. It means being loyal and true to someone, and keeping your promises. A faithful friend stays with you, even when it is hard.
explain: «The fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness, faithfulness, gentleness and self-control.» Faithfulness is one of the good qualities in this list. It sits between goodness and gentleness, so it names a kind of good character.
explain: Faithfulness can also mean staying true to a partner in marriage, or being exact and accurate, as when a copy stays faithful to the original book. Look at the words around it: the clues tell you which meaning fits.
fact: Faithfulness is a noun, and it is uncountable: you show faithfulness, or you have it.
fact: Faithfulness means being loyal and true, and keeping your promises.
fact: In the fruit of the Spirit, faithfulness is one of the qualities listed with love, joy, peace and kindness.
fact: Christians believe God's faithfulness means he keeps his promises and never leaves his people.
fact: Ruth and Noah are remembered in religion lessons for their faithfulness.
exercise: In «love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness, faithfulness, gentleness and self-control», which word means being loyal and true? | goodness | kindness | gentleness | *faithfulness
exercise: Ellie says faithfulness means being quick and good at sport. What does it really mean? | Being quick and good at sport | *Being loyal and true, and keeping your promises | Owning a lot of money | Being very loud when you speak
exercise: A dog stays beside its owner through hard times, year after year. Which quality does the dog show? | Speed | Greed | *Faithfulness | Sadness
test: In «faithfulness to a friend», what does faithfulness mean? | Forgetting your friend when things change | Winning every game with your friend | *Staying loyal and true to your friend | Being very quiet with your friend
test: A copy that is faithful to the original book is one that is: | Longer and more colourful | *Exact and accurate, like the original | Written in a different language
exam: Which statement about faithfulness is true? | It is a verb meaning to run fast | It is the name of a church building | *It is a noun that can mean loyalty, keeping promises, or being exact | It only means being happy
